{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/833639-custom-legends-and-lives","id":833639,"title":"Custom Legends and Lives","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-19T18:43:39-08:00","id":833639,"title":"Custom Legends and Lives","content":"I do enjoy Legends and Lives as an Anchor for Beasts. There is so much potential to explore with these traits, important as they are to a Beast. Unfortunately I find the number of examples provided to us in the corebook to be far too limited. I require more.<br /> <br /> So I'm here to ask if anyone has come up with new Legends and Lives to use for characters in their games, or can come up with them now. This first post would be used to compile a list for all of the ones mentioned here.<br /> <br /> Compilation!<br /> <br /> <b><u>Legends</u></b><br /> <b>Competitive:</b> Regain one point of Willpower if your character seeks out or answers a challenge against another. Regain all Willpower if doing so would be incredibly and obviously dangerous, such as accepting a Hero's challenge to single combat when he already placed an Anathema on you.<br /> <br /> <b>Deceitful: </b>Regain a point of Willpower when you trick another into a course of action that is potentially detrimental to them. Regain all Willpower when you trick an individual into a course of action that is detrimental to them when that individual has the power to take significant revenge upon you for the deception.<br /> <br /> <b>Implacable:</b> Regain one point of Willpower if your character pursues her Aspirations or Hunger even when doing so results in harm to herself. Regain all points of Willpower if this pursuit draws the attention of a Hero, or puts her loved ones at risk.<br /> <br /> <b>Repulsive: </b>Regain one point of Willpower when you shock others with your appearance and actions, while making them painfully aware you're not normal, such as eating rat heads in front of a a couple that's having a coffee. Regain all Willpower if this causes the disgust of people you care about or causes a threatening reaction, such as making yourself noticed by a Hero after scaring a bunch of the neighborhood's kids.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Lives</b></u><br /> <b>Curious: </b>Regain one point of Willpower when your thirst for knowledge makes you learn something new or interesting about the supernatural you would have not learned otherwise, such as staying after school to see who's carving enochian glyphs on the lockers. Regain all Willpower if you put yourself in a danger in order to get such knowledge or information with strictly mundane methods, such as breaking into a Hero's home without being aware of his current position in order to learn what he's got about your brood.<br /> <br /> <b>Flippant:</b> Regain one point of Willpower when you deal with a problem or face an obstacle without bringing your supernatural nature to bear even if it would be significantly easier. Regain all Willpower if you stand up to a Hero or another serious threat on human terms.<br /> <br /> <b>Wanderer: </b>Regain a point of Willpower when you find something on your wanderings that helps you solve a problem or answer a question. Regain all Willpower when you run from a problem in a way that leaves you or others in peril.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","user":"Aiden","date":". 02-23-2016, 06:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","tit